# ValeSpec — Function & Variable Naming Convention

## Core Rule

Every symbol at module scope uses the three-part double-underscore pattern:

```
ValeSpec__<ModuleName>__<PurposeOrRole>
```

- Segment 1: Always `ValeSpec` — never omitted
- Segment 2: The specific module name (see vocabulary below)
- Segment 3: PascalCase purpose/role
- Separator: Always `__` (double underscore) — never single underscore

---

## Functions

All named functions — public, private, helpers — use the three-part pattern. No `_` prefix for private functions.

```js
async function ValeSpec__ConfigLoader__LoadConfig() { ... }
function ValeSpec__ModeManager__HideAllPanels() { ... }      // private helper — no underscore prefix
function ValeSpec__StepManager__BuildProgressBar() { ... }
```

Local anonymous callbacks / one-liner event handlers may use camelCase.

---

## Module-Level Variables

All `let` / `const` at IIFE scope use the three-part pattern:

```js
let ValeSpec__StateManager__State       = { ... };
let ValeSpec__ModeManager__CurrentMode  = null;
const ValeSpec__ModeManager__ModePanelIds = { ... };
```

Simple scalar constants private to the IIFE use plain SCREAMING_SNAKE:

```js
const CONFIG_PATH = '...';
const SINGLE_WIDTH_THRESHOLD = 940;
```

Local variables **inside** function bodies use camelCase: `var configData`, `var panelId`.

---

## Public API Return Objects

IIFE return keys match the function name exactly. Callers use the full key:

```js
return {
    ValeSpec__ConfigLoader__LoadConfig : ValeSpec__ConfigLoader__LoadConfig,
    ValeSpec__ConfigLoader__GetSection : ValeSpec__ConfigLoader__GetSection
};

// caller:
window.ValeSpec__AppCore__ConfigLoader.ValeSpec__ConfigLoader__LoadConfig();
window.ValeSpec__AppCore__StateManager.ValeSpec__StateManager__On('modeChanged', fn);
```

---

## CSS Classes, IDs, and HTML

Both IDs and CSS classes use the same three-part convention:

```html
id="ValeSpec__App__NavigationBar"
id="ValeSpec__DocManagement__TableContainer"
class="ValeSpec__App__NavTab"
class="ValeSpec__App__ModePanel"
```

BEM modifiers append `--modifier`:

```html
class="ValeSpec__App__NavTab--active"
class="ValeSpec__DocManagement__RowBtn--delete"
class="ValeSpec__AssemblyEditor__StepPill--completed"
```

BEM sub-elements append `__SubElement` (PascalCase):

```html
class="ValeSpec__DocManagement__EmptyState__Title"
class="ValeSpec__AssemblyEditor__StepPill__Number"
```

---

## Module Segment Vocabulary (Segment 2)

### Window Registration — broader area as Segment 2
`window.ValeSpec__AppCore__StateManager`, `window.ValeSpec__SvgDrawing__RenderPipeline`, etc.

| Area | Window segment |
|---|---|
| App core bootstrap, mode routing, state, config | `AppCore` |
| Data & persistence | `AppData` |
| Utilities | `AppUtils`, `MathUtils` |
| SVG drawing engine | `SvgDrawing` |
| Document management mode | `DocManagement` |
| Assembly editor mode | `AssemblyEditor` |
| Document editor mode | `DocEditor` |
| Document preview mode | `DocPreview` |

